{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use the existing Spring XD module and plugin architecture to implement the Reactor stream processor and Protocol Buffer codec.",
    "Integrate a Zookeeper client within the xd-yarn script to query and retrieve the dynamically assigned admin port.",
    "Utilize Spring Integration message header manipulation to inject and track history metadata (stream name, module name).",
    "Develop the Ambari plugin following the standard Apache Ambari stack and service component architecture.",
    "Modify the JdbcHdfsOptionsMetadata to enforce mutual exclusivity of 'sql' and 'tableName' options and validate partitioned job definitions."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has prior experience with Spring XD, Java, YARN, and Hadoop ecosystems.",
    "Access to a YARN and Hadoop cluster is available for testing the xd-yarn script and Ambari plugin.",
    "Protocol Buffer schemas required for testing are either available or can be quickly defined.",
    "An existing CI/CD pipeline is in place to run automated tests and performance evaluations.",
    "The existing Spring XD codebase is well-structured and allows for straightforward extension points."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement xd-yarn info command",
      "activity_description": "Add an info command to the xd-yarn script that queries Zookeeper to retrieve and display the admin port for the current deployment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Reactor stream processor plugin",
      "activity_description": "Create a reactor based stream processor plugin similar to Spark and RxJava, allowing specification of the bare minimum (e.g., processor class) and exploring additional configuration via module option commands.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement history tracking in message headers",
      "activity_description": "Add an option to track history by injecting visibility data such as stream name and module name into the message header.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Protocol Buffer codec",
      "activity_description": "Add Google's Protocol Buffer codec option to serialize and deserialize objects based on its native specifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Add test coverage for complex objects",
      "activity_description": "Add test coverage for complex objects such as protocol buffers, nested variables, or object trees to evaluate and document performance characteristics.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Ambari plugin for Spring XD",
      "activity_description": "Develop an Ambari plugin to provision, manage, and monitor a Spring XD cluster using the same tool used for Hadoop clusters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Update wiki documentation for partitioned jobs",
      "activity_description": "Update the wiki to document how to create a job with 'partitions', explicitly including 'tableName' and 'columns', and call-out that 'sql' and 'tableName' are mutually exclusive. Document the logic in JdbcHdfsOptionsMetadata.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement partitioned job options",
      "activity_description": "Modify job definition logic to allow using either 'sql' or 'tableName' options, enabling partitioned jobs with a 'where' clause and strict table-column combo respectively.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 30
  }
}
```

